reating all cold operations as thin. Independent examination: four-commit source diff, driver, staged solve timing, sensor query scratch, TypeScript yields, mutation paths, distance import consumers, snapshot/hash code, native physics_world.c/solver.c/sensor.c/island.c and body/joint/shape referents. No rerun: findings follow directly from the code. Other dispositions: caller geometry builders/geometry math/compound are kept with the real world-independent authoring and JS geometry identity reason. CharacterPlugin is kept by explicit Scope exception. Snapshot codecs and hash observation are kept as requested serialization/observation over kernel bytes/records and opaque host values. Scalar helpers and fresh requested API values are legitimate bindings/observation. distance.ts is NOT shown to be a second production GJK home: its only non-test value consumer found is oracle/consumer.ts:12,290; API consumers import only ShapeProxy types. Keep it on the narrower independent reference/corpus reason, not on the claim that a public production distance algorithm needs TypeScript. Relocation/consolidation is an optional to-do, not evidence of a runtime second home. Notes/uncertainty: ascending touch pass, solve substage order, finalize after both joins, sensor minRange=16 and task-local header/stack/narrowphase points, and pool/material-only driver yields match the relevant native dependencies. Seven gold corrections are consistent with the recorded native float timestep/inverses and reaction scaling; endpoints were not independently rerun. Warmed JS path has no new per-step object construction; buffer growth still refreshes views. Existing island.rs:318-325,369-383 allocates fresh Vec scratch when the newly pooled split runs, unlike native island.c:414-417,528-559 reusable stack scratch; allocation checks of ordinary contact/sensor steps do not establish allocation-free split steps. This is pre-existing split code, not a new stage-9 allocator regression. Dead work: physics_